					<h1 class="title" title="Bondla Wildlife Sanctuary">Bondla Wildlife Sanctuary</h1>
					<div class="entry-content">
   <p><b>Location :</b> Located in Ponda Taluka in Central Goa, 20 kms from Mollem and 52 kms from Panaji.<br />
    <b>Area :</b> 8 sq. km<br />
    <b>Major Attractions : </b>Gaur, Sambar, Monkeys, Wild Boar, Langurs, Jackals<br />
    <b>Best Time to Visit :</b> October to March<br />
    <b>Timings :</b> 9.00 am to 5.00 pm, Thursday closed (Garden and Zoo)</p>
    

<h3>About Bondla Wildlife Sanctuary</h3>
<p>Bondla Wildlife Sanctuary is situated 52 km from Panaji in the foothills of the Western Ghats in Goa. Eight square km in size, Bondla is "rather small" even by official accounts. It includes a Mini Zoo, Deer Safari Park, Formal Gardens, Botanic Gardens and a few Ecotourism Cottages. 
    <img alt="bondla-wildlife-sanctuary Birds" title ="bondla-wildlife-sanctuary Birds"  class="thumb alignright"src="https://storage.googleapis.com/createweb/indiacitytrip.com/code/images/Bondla%20Wildlife%20Sanctuary/bird-wild.jpg" style="height:150px;width:200px;float:right" /></p>
    <p>The Forest Department has announced that it is contemplating to run a bus service from TISKA to BONDLA everyday, except Thursday. Dep. Tiska 11.00 hrs and 19.30 hrs Dep. Bondla 07.30 hrs and 17.45 hrs. Many currently travel via their own transport. Hired taxi is a "little bit costly" as the Forest Department cautions. &nbsp;</p>
    
    <h3>Sightseeing 
        <img alt="bondla-wildlife-lion" title ="bondla-wildlife-lion" style="height:150px;width:200px;float:right"  class="thumb alignright"
            src="https://storage.googleapis.com/createweb/indiacitytrip.com/code/images/Bondla%20Wildlife%20Sanctuary/bondla-wildlife-lion.jpg" /></h3>
    <p>There are botanical gardens, a zoo and a deer park. The gardens are very pleasant, while there has been some criticism of the state in which the animals are maintained. There are elephant rides offered in the afternoons, around 4PM.</p>
    <p>&nbsp;Late evenings and nights out there can be interesting. It has moist deciduous forests, small patches of evergreens, and Goa's state tree Terminalia Crenulata (Matti) and Rosewood are common here.

</p>
    <p>To see Goa's state animal, the gaur, you need to go here too. You could run into panther, jungle cat, leopard cat, toddy cat, deer, wild boars, porcupines, ant eaters, or squirrels are some of the other animals here. Over a hundred species of birds are believed to be here, and Goa's growing romance with British birdwatchers is building awareness in this area. 
        <img alt="bondla-wildlife-sanctuary-animals" title ="bondla-wildlife-sanctuary-animals" style="height:150px;width:200px;float:right"  class="thumb alignright"
            src="https://storage.googleapis.com/createweb/indiacitytrip.com/code/images/Bondla%20Wildlife%20Sanctuary/bondla-wildlife-sanctuary-animals.jpg" /></p>
        <p>    <b>*Zoological Park -</b> A tiny zoo in moated enclosures with natural surroundings. A few elephant, panther, lion, gaur, sambar, deers, sloth bear, porcupine, wild boar, crocodiles, and reptiles. </p>
    
    <p>    <b>*Deer Safari Park - </b>Visitors can move among deers in vehicles inside the Deer Safari Park housing sambar and spotted deers.</p>
    
    <p>    <b>*Formal Gardens -</b> Lawns, exotic trees, varieties of roses, and colourful flowering plants in the middle of the forest. 
        <img alt="leopard" title ="leopard" src="https://storage.googleapis.com/createweb/indiacitytrip.com/code/images/Bondla%20Wildlife%20Sanctuary/leopard-.jpg"   class="thumb alignright"style="height:150px;width:200px;float:right" /></p>
    <p>    <b>* Botanical Gardens -</b> Collection of plants.</p>
      <p>    <b>*Nature Education Centre - </b>Exhibits to see, feel and interpret. An attached library, with video movies screened on request. </p>
    
    <p>    <b>*Birdwatch -</b> Bondla is home to over a hundred bird species. For details on bird-watching areas contact the Park Range Office. </p>
    
    <p>    * See <b>wild animals </b>You need to scan from watch towers, to spy gaur, sambar, and wild boar at water-holes. You need luck too. 
        <img alt="wild-bear-Bondla" title ="wild-bear-Bondla" style="height:150px;width:200px;float:right"  class="thumb alignright"
            src="https://storage.googleapis.com/createweb/indiacitytrip.com/code/images/Bondla%20Wildlife%20Sanctuary/wild-bear-Bondla%20Wildlife%20Sanctuary.jpg" /></p>
    <p>    <b>*Nature trails - </b>For the more energetic. </p>
    
    <p>    <b>*Archaeological exhibit -</b> Deity Gajalaxmi with several motifs in bold relief, from the sixth to eighth century venerated by ancient settlers are located here. &nbsp;</p>
    <h3>How To reach</h3>
<p><b>By Road:</b> Bondla is off National Highway 4A that connects Belgaum with Panjim. Branch off at Mollem.</p>
    <br />
    <p>Route: Mollem-Satpal Sancorda-Shivddem-Bondla. (20 kms). Branch off at Tiska Route: Tiska - Usgaon - Ganhem - Bondla (14 kms).</p>
<p>Route: Margao-Ponda-Usgao-Ganjem-Bondla (36 kms) Panjim-Ponda-Usgao-Ganjem-Bondla (52 kms).<img 
        alt="tiger-wildlife-tour" title ="tiger-wildlife-tour" src="https://storage.googleapis.com/createweb/indiacitytrip.com/code/images/Bondla%20Wildlife%20Sanctuary/tiger-wildlife-tour.jpg"   class="thumb alignright" style="height:150px;width:200px;float:right"  /></p>
    
<p><b>By Rail: </b>Collem (on the Mormugao-Hubli line). Route: Collem-Mollem-Sancorda-Shivddem-Bondla: 28 kms.</p>
<p>Carambolim (Karmali Railway Station, on Konkan Railway) Route: Carambolim-Old Goa-Ponda-Usgao-Ganjem-Bondla: 40 kms.</p>
    
<p><b>By Air:</b> Dabolim-Ponda-Usgao-Ganjem-Bondla (70 kms) </p>
